- Access administration features according to permissions.

The system must protect financial information and preserve the correctness of all accounting records.

## 1.3 Rules that must never be violated

1. Do not use Python anywhere in the approved application architecture.
2. Do not replace PHP with another backend language.
3. Do not replace MySQL with another primary database without approval.
4. Do not replace the approved C++ analytics component with Python.
5. Do not put all application logic into one PHP file.
6. Do not generate an incomplete application and call it complete.
7. Do not skip database migrations.
8. Do not skip financial correctness tests.
9. Do not skip authorization testing.
10. Do not invent financial information.
11. Do not use floating-point database types for authoritative monetary values.
12. Do not allow posted financial transactions to be silently overwritten.
13. Do not count transfers as income or expenses.
14. Do not allow analytics to create, post, edit or reverse financial records.
15. Do not trust frontend-only permissions.
16. Do not expose passwords, database credentials or application secrets.
17. Do not store private financial documents in publicly accessible directories.
18. Do not silently remove existing working functionality.
19. Do not declare a feature complete before its acceptance criteria pass.
20. Do not deploy an unverified financial application as production-ready.

