## 18.1 Performance

- Paginate large tables.
- Optimize database queries.
- Add appropriate indexes.
- Avoid unnecessary queries.
- Load dashboard data efficiently.
- Optimize exports.
- Limit analytics process execution.
- Avoid loading all historical transactions at once.
- Cache only where safe.
- Invalidate summaries after relevant financial changes.

Define performance targets using a documented workload and verify them using tests. Do not invent performance results.

## 18.2 Reliability

- Handle database connection failures.
- Handle failed background jobs.
- Handle C++ analytics timeouts.
- Handle duplicate requests.
- Handle network interruptions.
- Preserve committed financial records.
- Use database transactions.
- Maintain logs without exposing secrets.

## 18.3 Backup and restoration

